# Everything listed here is excluded from the BUILD CONTEXT — the tar of this
# directory that `docker build .` uploads to the builder before it reads the
# first instruction in the Dockerfile.
#
# Without this file the context is ~900 MB, almost all of it target/ and the
# uploaded images, and every build pays to send it. With it the context is a
# couple of MB.
#
# It is also a correctness control, not only a speed one. target/ holds classes
# compiled by the JDK on THIS machine; letting them into the context risks the
# build reusing them instead of compiling fresh, which is how "it works locally"
# becomes an image nobody can reproduce.

# Build output — the image compiles its own.
target/

# The wrapper downloads this on first run. It is gitignored, and a jar copied
# from the host is one more thing that might not match the wrapper properties.
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# Uploaded product images. Runtime data, not source.
uploads/

# ⚠️ Secrets. application-local.properties holds real Stripe test keys and the
# JWT signing secret. A file copied into an image is in a layer FOREVER — you
# cannot delete it in a later instruction, because the layer that added it is
# still there and `docker history` will hand it to anyone who pulls the image.
src/main/resources/application-local.properties
src/main/resources/application-*.local.properties
.env
.env.local

# Editor and VCS noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Not needed to build, and changing one would bust the cache for no reason.
HELP.md
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
